column2:
I shall not eat on Vishnu's day, nor shall I kill my son, good lady. I shall tear myself open, and Goddess Sandhyavali too,
naradapuran:157:34	or do some other dreadful deed at your command. Give up this wicked obsession about my son, fair-browed one.
naradapuran:157:35	What fruit will you have by killing my son Dharmangada? What is the gain in eating on Vishnu's day? Tell me.
naradapuran:157:36	I am your servant, your menial, under your control, fair-faced one. Ask another boon, fair one; I have come to you for refuge.
naradapuran:157:37	Equal to a red ashoka... in all ways I shall do any other task of yours; I am in your power.
naradapuran:157:38	Be gracious to me, goddess; give me the alms of a son. A virtuous son is hard to get; Hari's day is hard to get;
naradapuran:157:39	Ganga water is hard to get; a mother on earth is hard to get; birth in a good family is hard to get; a wife of good lineage is hard to get;
naradapuran:157:40	a gift of gold is hard to get; worship of Hari is hard to get; Vaishnava initiation is hard to get; a collection of Smriti is hard to get;
naradapuran:157:41	living in Shukara (Varaha-kshetra) is hard to get; meditation on Hari is hard to get; a vigil of Vishnu is hard to get; honouring oneself is hard to get;
naradapuran:157:42	obtaining a son is hard to get; Pushkara water is hard to get; the company of the good is hard to get; devotion, it is said, is hard to get;
naradapuran:157:43	the gift of a tawny cow is hard to get; the release of a blue bull is hard to get; shraddha done on the thirteenth is hard to get, fair-hued one;
naradapuran:157:44	land is hard to get; a vow completed, destroying sin, is hard to get; a sesame cow going to a Brahmin, fair-browed one, is hard to get;
naradapuran:157:45	bathing in amalaka, fair-hipped one, is hard to get; Hari's day is hard to get; bathing in cool water at the time of parvan is hard to get,
naradapuran:157:46	especially in the month of Magha at the auspicious time of dawn; the rite performed as the scripture prescribes, goddess, is hard to get on earth;
naradapuran:157:47	welfare and wholesome things are hard to get, and medicine; the removal of disease by the way of the scripture is hard to get;
naradapuran:157:48	the remembrance of Vishnu at death, fair-hued one, is hard to get. So, fair-hipped one, do my word, protecting dharma.
naradapuran:157:49	What is the use of killing, fair-limbed one? You should show favour. The pleasures have been enjoyed well, the kingdom made free of thorns.
naradapuran:157:50	I have placed my foot on the head of the protectors of gods, cows and Brahmins. I shall never kill the son whom I have not even seen with desires.
naradapuran:157:51	With my own hand, fair-limbed one — what sin is greater than this? Mohini said: "Dharmangada is not my enemy; I do not kill your son.
